# CODE + QUESTION ON THE UNIVERSAL ANSWER PLAN — gen396.
#
# The conditional plan proved that one turn's typed spans compose a response
# entirely in the KB.  A statement trace followed by a question is the SECOND
# instance of that substrate, not a second parser: the trace span carries a
# state, the query span carries an obligation, and the KB joins them.
#
# The join is what the ratchet is about.  The historical consumer picked the
# LAST identifier-shaped token of the question and asked the evaluator about it,
# so a question that ends on an ordinary word lost a binding it had named.  The
# plan instead keeps every candidate the question mentions and every binding the
# trace produced, and lets the two sets meet: the reading is the identifier the
# trace actually binds.  One reading answers, several stay several.

[mock live]
!set PARROT0_BASE=kb/core/base.p0
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_WORLD_FACTS=1
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test the answered binding is the one the trace binds, not the last word]
> total=3; total += 4; what is total in the end
< 7.
> a=2; b=5; a++; what is b
< 5.
> int x=4; x *= 3; what is x
< 12.

[test a question naming no binding of the trace is a typed gap, not a number]
> total=3; total += 4; what is the outcome
<! 7.
<~ none of the names

[test an update without an initial binding is still not fabricated]
> i++; what is i
<! 1.

[test two named bindings stay two readings instead of one silent pick]
> a=2; b=5; what is a and b
<! 2.
<! 5.
<~ which binding

# The ablation uses the ambiguous stimulus on purpose: with the state model off
# the turn falls back to the historical consumer, which picks the last named
# identifier and answers 5 — so the difference the ratchet observes is the MOVE,
# not the number.
[test the state model of a span role grows and ablates at runtime]
!forget span_state_model(code, statement_trace)
> a=2; b=5; what is a and b
<! which binding
!assert span_state_model(code, statement_trace)
> a=2; b=5; what is a and b
<~ which binding

[test a query cue taught at runtime reaches the same plan]
> q=5; q *= 3; final register q
<! 15.
!assert segment_role(query, "final register")
> q=5; q *= 3; final register q
< 15.
!forget segment_role(query, "final register")
> q=5; q *= 3; final register q
<! 15.
